events.body:
@xHope-tech 
Thank you for your contribution! However, I believe the documentation is fine as is. X11 is ubiquitous in the Linux world. Moreover, the following sentence refers to "runtime library dependencies", which implies that X11 also refers to the protocol implementation rather than the protocol itself. Therefore, it's okay to keep simply "X11".

Also, the branch should not contain any merge commits.

@diegoviola:
> This isn't wrong, but I think the whole ("and uses the `xcb` QPA (Qt Platform Abstraction) platform plugin to run on X11") could be dropped. `bitcoin-qt` runs fine with the `wayland` plugin as well.

That holds for builds against distro Qt packages, but `doc/INSTALL_linux.md` is shipped as `INSTALL.md` in the Linux release packages, and the `wayland` plugin is not compiled into those binaries, only `xcb` is available. So the current sentence is accurate for its audience.
